  "provenance": "derived",
  "notes": [
    "request.frames are sent in order after connecting; response.frames lists what the client must receive, in order.",
    "Each expected frame has delivery \"direct\" (a reply to this client) or \"broadcast\" (sent to every client, at most INTERFACE_UPDATE_COOLDOWN = 1000 ms after the change).",
    "A text frame only gets a direct reply when no broadcast is pending: a frame that changes state is answered by the broadcast instead (ws.cpp: `if (!interfaceUpdateCallMode)`).",
    "\"none\" means nothing may arrive within 1500 ms."
  ],
